    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2e8fdd06-0a77-520b-9775-196c4f15892c",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -7 & -3 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -7 & -3 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $D,E,$ and $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $E$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, and $F$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $D$ and $3$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $D$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $D$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{D}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $F$ and $3$ rows in $E.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ equals the number of rows in $E,$ the matrices $F$ and $E$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{E}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $E$ and $D$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{D}_{2\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe products $DF$ and $FE$ are well defined. The product $ED$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "402d1bee-0098-50d2-ba90-dfb788f4f8ed",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $DF$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
